---
import Navigation from "../../components/navigation.astro";
import { posts } from "../../data/posts.js";

const post = posts.find((post) => post.slug === "post_eight");

if (!post) {
  throw new Error("Blog post not found.");
}

const { title, date, tags } = post;
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>{title} | Ivy Duncan</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content={post.excerpt}
    />
  </head>

  <body>
    <Navigation />

    <main>
      <article class="blog-post">
        <div class="container narrow">
          <header class="post-header">
            <p class="eyebrow">From the Blog</p>

            <h1>{title}</h1>

            <p class="post-date">{date}</p>

            <div class="post-tags">
              {tags.map((tag) => (
                <a
                  href={`/blog/tag/${tag.toLowerCase().replace(/\s+/g, "-")}`}
                  class="post-tag"
                >
                  {tag}
                </a>
              ))}
            </div>
          </header>

          <div class="post-content">
            <h2>Friday Writing Recap</h2>

            <p>
              I think I'm going to use Friday posts to share a brief writing
              recap of the week. Now, anyone who has been following me for a
              while knows that I'm not exactly great at keeping up with blogs,
              accounts, and things like that (I almost never post on my
              Instagram). But I'm hoping that, for as long as I'm able to keep
              up with regular blog posts, sharing weekly writing updates will
              keep me accountable and help motivate me when I need a push (or
              two) to get past writer's block.
            </p>

            <p>This week:</p>

            <ul>
              <li>
                I finished reading and marking up my first physical copy of
                <em>Not Interested</em>. This is good, since editing starts in
                just two weeks, and I want to make all these fixes before
                sending the file off to my editor.
              </li>

              <li>
                I didn't get much writing done since I was so focused on
                reading, but I think I'm going to go over what I have for Book
                Four from the beginning. My reread of <em>Not Interested</em> gave 
                me some ideas for adjustments I could make to the story
                for Book Four.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <p>That's it for this week!</p>
          </div>

          <footer class="post-footer">
            <a href="/blog" class="back-link">← Back to the blog</a>
          </footer>
        </div>
      </article>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <div class="container">
        <p>© {new Date().getFullYear()} Ivy Duncan. All rights reserved.</p>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .container {
    width: min(1100px, calc(100% - 3rem));
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .narrow {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .blog-post {
    padding: 5rem 0;
  }

  .post-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #765f48;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .post-header h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .post-date {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    color: #6f6a63;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .post-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .post-tag {
    color: #765f48;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .post-tag:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .post-content {
    color: #3f3a35;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .post-content p {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .post-content strong {
    color: #765f48;
  }

  .post-content ul {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .post-content li {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .post-footer {
    margin-top: 4rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #ddd6cd;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: #765f48;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .site-footer {
    padding: 2rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #ddd6cd;
    color: #6f6a63;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .container {
      width: min(100% - 2rem, 1100px);
    }

    .blog-post {
      padding: 3.5rem 0;
    }
  }
</style>